	title = {Quantum-Resistant Blockchain: Enhancing Blockchain Security with Round5},
	year = {2025},
	journal = {2025 IEEE 7th International Conference on Sustainable Technologies For Industry 5.0, STI 2025},
	pages = {},
	doi = {10.1109/STI69347.2025.11367567},
	url = {https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105033997051?origin=resultslist},
	affiliations = {Mymensingh Engineering College, Dept. of Computer Science and Engineering, Mymensingh, Bangladesh; Jatiya Kabi Kazi Nazrul Islam University, Dept. of Computer Science and Engineering, Mymensingh, Bangladesh; Abo Akademi University, Faculty of Science and Engineering, Finland; North South University, Department of Electrical and Computer Engineering, Bangladesh},
	abstract = {Traditional cryptographic techniques that form the basis of blockchain security are becoming more vulnerable to quantum attacks as a result of the development of quantum computers. With an emphasis on the Round5 algorithm, this paper explores the use of quantum-resistant cryptographic algorithms to strengthen blockchain security systems. Round5 operates as an all-purpose, secure, low-complexity cryptosystem with guaranteed security levels against both classical and quantum threats that will be found sustaining technological evolution in the future; therefore, without such an adjustment, all blockchain improvements will be at risk in the future. Firstly, our study involves an in-depth understanding of how blockchain relies on cryptography for secure transactions and privacy. Second, it involves the potentially disruptive benefits of quantum computing and its ability to hack current cryptographic solutions. Finally, it involves the potential for ROUND5, a lattice-based cryptographic solution, is to be integrated into a blockchain for better safety and operation. In this respect, we propose a quantum-resistant blockchain architecture to provide better safety without any drastic operational shortcomings. The quantum-resilient nature inspires confidence in this blockchain application for current and future technological use. To confirm the effectiveness and resilience of the suggested method, the main parameters of key performance, such as key generation time, the efficiency of encapsulation and decapsulation, the size of keys, and quantum security levels under the NIST standards, undergo testing. Β© 2025 IEEE.},
	author_keywords = {blockchain security; decentralized ledger; lattice-based cryptography; post-quantum cryptography; public key infrastructure (PKI); Quantum-resistant system; round5},
