	affiliations = {Department of Network and Information Security, School of Cyber Science and Engineering, Huazhong University of Science and Technology, Hubei, Wuhan, 430074, China},
	abstract = {Ensuring the information security and privacy of users in the Internet of Vehicles (IoV) is crucial for gaining user trust and promoting the application of vehicular networks. This article designs an efficient linkable ring signature (LRS) scheme on the basis of the middle-product learning with errors (MP-LWE) problem and applies it to vehicular networks to resist quantum computer attacks. First, a new authentication scheme based on the MP-LWE problem is proposed. In addition, it is demonstrated to be compatible with the DualRing framework. Then, according to the transformation of DualRing, a new efficient ring signature scheme based on the MP-LWE problem is obtained. With anti-collision hash functions to assign a specific tag to each user, this ring signature scheme is converted into a secure LRS scheme. Subsequently, under the random oracle model, the unforgeability, anonymity, and linkability of the LRS scheme are shown. Furthermore, by integrating the scheme constructed in this article with blockchain technology and applying it to IoV scenarios, it effectively ensures the privacy of vehicle identities during communication and the reliability of messages and significantly improves communication efficiency. The signature length of the LRS scheme designed in the present study is 4β€“20 times shorter than that of similar schemes. Regarding time overhead, the total time overhead of our scheme can be reduced by 14.72%β€“40.38%. Copyright Β© 2025 Lansheng Han et al. IET Information Security published by John Wiley & Sons Ltd.},
