	abstract = {Blockchain technology has emerged as a revolutionary paradigm for secure and transparent transactions in decentralized networks. As the adoption of blockchain continues to grow, so does the sophistication of malicious actors seeking to exploit vulnerabilities within this distributed ledger system. This research chapter delves into the dynamic landscape of attacks targeting blockchain networks and investigates the corresponding defense mechanisms. The chapter provides a comprehensive analysis of various attack vectors, ranging from 51% attacks to smart contract vulnerabilities, highlighting the potential threats to the integrity and confidentiality of blockchain data. Additionally, it examines the implications of novel attack strategies such as quantum attacks on cryptographic primitives used in blockchain. In response to these challenges, the research identifies and evaluates existing defense mechanisms and countermeasures employed by the blockchain community. This includes consensus algorithms, cryptographic protocols, and secure coding practices designed to fortify the resilience of blockchain networks against adversarial activities. Furthermore, the chapter explores the ongoing research and development efforts in the field, including emerging technologies like homomorphic encryption and post-quantum cryptography, aiming to enhance the security posture of blockchain systems in the face of evolving threats. By synthesizing insights from both the attack and defense perspectives, this chapter contributes to a deeper understanding of the complex cybersecurity landscape surrounding blockchain technology. The findings offer valuable insights for practitioners, researchers, and policymakers engaged in securing the future of decentralized systems. Β© 2026 selection and editorial matter, Dileep Kumar Murala, Sandeep Kumar Panda, and Sujata Priyambada Dash; individual chapters, the contributors. All rights reserved.},
