	affiliations = {School of Information Technology, Vivekananda Institute of Professional Studies - Technical Campus, New Delhi, India},
	abstract = {The quick development of blockchain technology has completely changed the way safe and transparent transactions are conducted. Nevertheless, the cryptographic foundations supporting these systems confront never-before-seen issues with the impending arrival of quantum computing. The critical function that Post-Quantum Cryptography (PQC) plays in strengthening blockchain networks is examined in this chapter. Leading PQC techniques include lattice-based, code-based, and multivariate polynomial cryptography, which use complex mathematical structures to fend off future quantum attacks. PQC research is taking place against a practical background, which includes the performance consequences and compatibility issues that come with integrating PQC into blockchain systems. Although quantum-resistant security has great promise, the chapter emphasises the necessity of standardised solutions to guarantee smooth adoption across various blockchain systems. A few use cases are also included in the chapter where PQC might be very important. The chapter ends with a vision of a day where post-quantum cryptography (PQC) is essential to blockchain security and emphasises the need to adopt PQC in a proactive manner. It frames this development as a necessary first step towards building a blockchain environment that is resistant to quantum errors and goes beyond the bounds of both quantum qubits and classical bits. Β© 2025},
