cs. First, industry-specific challenges related to real-time fault detection, optimization, and security are identified. Advanced AI-driven models, such as random forest, fuzzy Minβ€“Max (FMM), and deep learning techniques, are employed for anomaly detection in electromechanical components like actuators, motors, and gearboxes. Hybrid cloud-edge architectures powered by 6G ensure real-time fault reporting, leveraging secure blockchain frameworks for tamper-proof logging of device failures. As 6G technology matures, IoT networks expand, and QC hardware advances, the transition from reactive maintenance to AI- and QC-driven proactive fault prevention will redefine consumer electronics, making them smarter, more secure, and energy-efficient. Future advancements in digital twins, quantum-enhanced AI, AI-powered self-healing systems, and resilient IoT architectures will drive the next generation of intelligent consumer electronics, ensuring long-term sustainability, performance optimization, and real-time adaptability. Β© 2026 selection and editorial matter, Sushil Kumar Singh, Rajendrasinh B. Jadeja, Ashish Khanna, Pushan Kumar Dutta, and Bal Virdee; individual chapters, the contributors.},
