	affiliations = {Pranveer Singh Institute of Technology, Department of Computer Science & Engineering, Kanpur, India},
	abstract = {The robustness and consistency of cryptographic keys are essential components that determine the security for cryptographic systems. This study provides a thorough analysis of important authentication strategies and highlights their critical function in enhancing digital communication security and data security. We begin by elucidating the significance of key authentication as a critical component in safeguarding sensitive information. In an era marked by growing cyber threats, ensuring the authenticity and reliability of cryptographic keys is paramount. The paper provides a comprehensive survey of key authentication methods, ranging from traditional approaches like password-based authentication to advanced techniques such as biometrics, multifactor authentication, and hardware security modules. Each method is critically evaluated for its strengths, weaknesses, and suitability in diverse applications. Furthermore, this research explores practical implementations of key authentication in real-world scenarios. We investigate secure messaging protocols, data encryption, and access control systems, highlighting how key authentication strengthens security in these contexts. The evolving landscape of cryptography is also addressed, with insights into emerging trends like post-quantum cryptography and blockchain-based authentication. These innovations promise to reshape the future of key authentication and data security. This study emphasizes how important key authentication is to the field of cryptography. By advancing our understanding of these techniques and their practical applications, we contribute to fortifying the foundations of secure digital communication in an increasingly interconnected world.  Β© 2024 IEEE.},
	author_keywords = {Cryptographic Keys; Data Security; Digital Communication; Key Authentication},
