	abstract = {The technology sector has seen incredible growth and development over the past few years. Dubbed as 'Industry 4.0', the proliferation of innovative technologies such as Artificial Intelligence, Blockchain, cutting-edge devices, Quantum Computing, self-driving vehicles, Machine Learning, Virtual and Augmented Reality, Extended Reality, the Enterprise Metaverse, and the Internet of Things have dramatically impacted the world. This article explores how these advancements affect the service industry, such as banking, insurance, and agriculture. It provides a comprehensive overview of integrating these emerging technologies into the service industry, an analysis of their impact and a general framework for adoption. The completion of fifth generation mobile network (5G) rollout will bring about a shift from smartphones to advanced wearables in the next five years, with Augmented Reality (AR) glasses leading the way and propelling the global economy forward. Artificial Intelligence (AI), robotics, and other cutting-edge technologies have something to offer for every service industry. They can drive new business growth, increase revenue, improve differentiation, reduce operational costs, manage risks, and enhance customer experience. In conclusion, this article provides a glimpse into the present and future of the service industry through the lens of emerging technologies and their ability to shape it for the better. Β© 2023 Bharati Vidyapeeth, New Delhi.},
